# NAME

tinydb.conf - TinyDB configuration file

# SYNOPSIS

/etc/tinydb/tinydb.conf

# DESCRIPTION

TinyDB configuration file uses a simple key=value format. Lines starting
with # are comments.

# CONFIGURATION OPTIONS

## Server Options

port = *number*
:   TCP port for client connections. Default: 5432.

socket_path = *path*
:   Unix domain socket path. Default: /run/tinydb/tinydb.sock.

max_connections = *number*
:   Maximum number of concurrent connections. Default: 64.

## Storage Options

data_dir = *path*
:   Database data directory. Default: /var/lib/tinydb.

cache_size = *number*
:   Page cache size in pages. Default: 256.

## WAL Options

wal_autocheckpoint = *true|false*
:   Enable automatic WAL checkpoint. Default: true.

wal_threshold = *number*
:   Number of writes before auto-checkpoint. Default: 1000.

## Logging Options

log_level = *debug|info|warn|error*
:   Log level. Default: info.

log_path = *path*
:   Log file path. Default: /var/log/tinydb/tinydb.log.

# EXAMPLE

```
# TinyDB Configuration
port = 5432
socket_path = /run/tinydb/tinydb.sock
data_dir = /var/lib/tinydb
cache_size = 256
wal_autocheckpoint = true
wal_threshold = 1000
log_level = info
```

# FILES

/etc/tinydb/tinydb.conf
:   Main configuration file.

